-- title:
--   Kernel of the ∞-reduction map is killed by Uₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field that is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and let $S$ be a set of natural numbers. Write [`CuspForm.IntTwoCuspForms M H p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L374) for the quotient of the two-cusp integral lattice [`CuspForm.twoCuspLattice M H 2 p ⊥`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L86) — built from the weight-two cusp forms $f$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) all of whose Hecke translates $tf$ have $q$-coefficients in the prime subring of $\mathbb{C}$ at every index, both for $tf$ and for its weight-two slash by every Atkin–Lehner datum at $p$ — by the submodule generated by `intIdeal p`. Let $\rho$ be a $K$-linear map from $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}$ `IntTwoCuspForms M H p` to the module of Kähler differentials over $K$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH (M/p) (ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M H hpM))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), where `infSubgroup` is the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$; assume $\rho$ satisfies [`ModularCurve.IsInfReductionMap`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L443), i.e. for every weight-two cusp form $f$ in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p ⊥`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54) and every integral power series $p_f$ whose complex image is the $q$-expansion of $f$, applying `diffQExp` to $\rho(1 \otimes \overline{f})$ gives the Laurent series `intSeriesC K` $p_f$. Then every $x$ in $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}$ `IntTwoCuspForms M H p` with $\rho x = 0$ is annihilated by the base change to $K$ of the operator [`CuspForm.intTwoCuspGenMod M H p S (CohCarrier.Gen.U p _ hpM)`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L418), the mod $p$ operator $U_p$ on the two-cusp integral lattice.
--
--   This is the assertion that a mod $p$ weight-two form of level $\Gamma_H(M)$, $M = Np$, whose associated differential vanishes on the component of the special fibre through the cusp $\infty$ is killed by $U_p$ — the step "if $\omega = 0$ on $\Sigma^\mu$ then $U_p\omega = 0$" of Wiles's analysis of the two-component special fibre, here for the whole space rather than a single eigenspace. It is used in the construction of the injection of the two-cusp form space into the dual of the multiplicative part of the Tate module at an ordinary prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IsInfReductionMap_baseChange_genU_self_apply_eq_zero_of_apply_eq_zero.lean

